        ],
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "header",
        "text": "UNITED NATIONS CONFERENCE ON TRADE AND DEVELOPMENT",
        "bbox": [
            230,
            15,
            767,
            35
        ],
        "page_idx": 0
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Introduction",
        "text_level": 2,
        "bbox": [
            94,
            73,
            434,
            127
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The reopening of the Strait of Hormuz would bring much-needed relief for many economies.",
        "bbox": [
            90,
            170,
            854,
            247
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This is a first step toward a progressive recovery of energy markets and international trade.",
        "bbox": [
            90,
            257,
            888,
            333
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "However, during more than 100 days of shipping disruption, negative effects have already rippled through the global economy.",
        "bbox": [
            90,
            342,
            909,
            457
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Vulnerable economies have been particularly exposed to oil and fertilizer price shocks. These shocks can result in persistent inflation.",
        "bbox": [
            90,
            466,
            863,
            580
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "People suffer from inflation, especially the poor. It squeezes household budgets and makes necessities—such as food and healthcare—less affordable.",
        "bbox": [
            90,
            589,
            931,
            703
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The reopening paves the way for recovery. But for vulnerable economies, the path can be longer, uneven and costly. International support is needed to improve their ability to cope.",
        "bbox": [
            89,
            713,
            911,
            866
        ],
        "page_idx": 1
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "After 100+ days of disruption, trade through the Strait is set to resume.",
        "text_level": 2,
        "bbox": [
            156,
            62,
            851,
            155
        ],
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Daily ship transits through the Strait of Hormuz in 2026",
        "bbox": [
            156,
            173,
            846,
            210
        ],
        "page_idx": 2
    },
    {
        "type": "chart",
        "img_path": "images/bbc75ee7b9f97de136de90770d7df917b4308357c65861fabc80c2307baa6340.jpg",
        "content": "",
        "chart_caption": [],
        "chart_footnote": [
            "Source: UN Trade and Development, based on Clarksons Research Shipping Intelligence Network.\nNote: Ship transits between 1 January and 27 June 2026."
        ],
        "bbox": [
            61,
