        ],
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "page_number",
        "text": "10",
        "bbox": [
            914,
            962,
            934,
            978
        ],
        "page_idx": 9
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Trade shocks hit hardest where the ability to cope is limited.",
        "text_level": 1,
        "bbox": [
            154,
            122,
            841,
            214
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Tighter public finances mean less room to cushion shocks, especially when vulnerable countries face",
        "bbox": [
            131,
            233,
            865,
            302
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "difficulties to mobilize resources, domestically or externally,",
        "bbox": [
            212,
            407,
            760,
            482
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "a heavy debt servicing burden and exchange rate risks associated with high levels of external debt,",
        "bbox": [
            212,
            515,
            837,
            622
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "a drop in remittances that could cut off a financial lifeline for some economies,",
        "bbox": [
            212,
            657,
            833,
            728
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "declining international aid.",
        "bbox": [
            212,
            763,
            661,
            800
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "header",
        "text": "",
        "bbox": [
            457,
            29,
            540,
            105
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "page_number",
        "text": "11",
        "bbox": [
            913,
            962,
            932,
            978
        ],
        "page_idx": 10
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Short-lived energy shocks can have long-term consequences",
        "text_level": 2,
        "bbox": [
            117,
            358,
            865,
            691
        ],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "page_number",
        "text": "12",
        "bbox": [
            915,
            963,
            934,
            977
        ],
        "page_idx": 11
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "In a fragile global economy, energy shocks fuel lasting higher inflation.",
        "text_level": 2,
        "bbox": [
            157,
            63,
            848,
            154
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Impact of a 1 per cent change in energy prices on inflation, in per cent",
        "bbox": [
            63,
            169,
            941,
            204
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "chart",
        "img_path": "images/9f62975ede09805bbbd2164a9a898b1fb7d8192650f5fe1fc0aabf40f4668dcd.jpg",
        "content": "",
        "chart_caption": [],
        "chart_footnote": [
            "Source: UN Trade and Development (UNCTAD), based on IMF, Patrick Imam and Tigran Poghosyan (2026)."
        ],
        "bbox": [
            70,
            239,
            920,
            785
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Note: Cumulative impact on inflation based on the consumer price index. Estimates based on 70 advanced and emerging economies. All coefficients were statistically significantly different from zero, based on a $95\\%$ confidence interval with robust standard errors.",
        "bbox": [
            62,
            866,
            930,
            937
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "header",
        "text": ">",
        "bbox": [
            65,
            64,
            143,
            146
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "page_number",
        "text": "13",
        "bbox": [
            913,
            962,
            934,
            978
        ],
        "page_idx": 12
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Food price inflation may keep climbing even after the triggering shock fades.",
        "text_level": 1,
        "bbox": [
            157,
            62,
            868,
            154
        ],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Year-on-year food price inflation rate in developing countries, median by country group",
        "bbox": [
            63,
            169,
            828,
            239
        ],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "chart",
        "img_path": "images/7f6ac2fae94ea76f0b820f7c6e990336c4d08ad09da651c994bbd6b2a3185055.jpg",
        "content": "",
        "chart_caption": [],
        "chart_footnote": [
            "Source: UN Trade and Development (UNCTAD), based on national sources and OECD retrieved from LSEG Data & Analytics.",
            "Note: Based on the consumer price index for food and beverages. Between 2020 and 2024, food prices were driven by a combination of COVID-19 inflation, the war in Ukraine and climate shocks. The depicted data covers 82 developing countries, 21 LDCs and 10 SIDS."
        ],
        "bbox": [
            69,
            248,
            915,
            787
        ],
        "page_idx": 13
    },
    {
        "type": "header",
        "text": ">",
        "bbox": [
            65,
            64,
